Hi Chris, when it says "undefined reference" in your previous message,
it seems to not be finding C++ functions and classes that should be
present in files in
C:\Users\chjennel\Documents\R\win-library\4.0\nimble\include\nimble,
even though the "-I" flag should be telling the compiler to look
there.

Can you list out the files (and their sizes) in
C:\Users\chjennel\Documents\R\win-library\4.0\nimble\include\nimble,
and in your response show what those are? I'm wondering if those files
are messed up somehow.

Chris

On Wed, Apr 29, 2020 at 1:40 PM Christopher Jennelle <cjen...@umn.edu> wrote:
>
> I can only guess that there is some kind of PATH problem, but I cannot figure it out. From the error given below, it looks like R is having trouble finding a nimble-generated code called "P_4_code_MID_4_04_29_15_33_58.dll" - I did a system search for this dll file (via Sys.which("P_4_code_MID_4_04_29_15_33_58.dll") and it doesn't exist. Not sure if it even should exist?
